<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8" />
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
<title>SlayZone Multi-Hub Federation — Architecture</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0e1117;
    --panel: #161b22;
    --panel-2: #1c232d;
    --ink: #e6edf3;
    --muted: #8b98a9;
    --line: #30363d;
    --client: #4c8dff;   /* desktop client */
    --local: #2ea043;    /* local hub */
    --remote: #14b8a6;   /* remote hub */
    --runner: #d29922;   /* runner exec node */
    --auth: #a371f7;     /* auth / security */
    --danger: #f85149;
    --radius: 12px;
    font-synthesis: none;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: light) {
    :root {
      --bg: #f6f8fa; --panel: #ffffff; --panel-2: #f0f3f6;
      --ink: #1f2328; --muted: #59636e; --line: #d0d7de;
    }
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink);
    font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    line-height: 1.5; padding: 32px 20px 64px;
  }
  .wrap { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; }
  h1 { font-size: 22px; margin: 0 0 4px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .sub { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; margin: 0 0 24px; }
  .legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 14px; margin: 0 0 28px; font-size: 12px; }
  .legend span { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; color: var(--muted); }
  .dot { width: 11px; height: 11px; border-radius: 3px; display: inline-block; }

  .col-labels { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .col-labels div { text-align: center; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }

  .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px; align-items: start; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .grid, .col-labels { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  .card {
    background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 14px; position: relative;
  }
  .card h2 { font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 2px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
  .card .tag { font-size: 10.5px; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 500; }
  .card .body { margin-top: 10px; display: grid; gap: 8px; }

  .chip {
    background: var(--panel-2); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 8px 10px; font-size: 12px;
  }
  .chip b { font-weight: 600; }
  .chip .k { color: var(--muted); font-size: 11px; display: block; margin-top: 2px; }
  code { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 11px; background: rgba(127,127,127,.15); padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 4px; }

  .edge {
    border-left: 3px solid; padding-left: 10px; font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--muted);
    margin: 6px 0;
  }
  .accent-client { border-color: var(--client); }
  .accent-local  { border-color: var(--local); }
  .accent-remote { border-color: var(--remote); }
  .accent-runner { border-color: var(--runner); }
  .accent-auth   { border-color: var(--auth); }
  .bar { height: 4px; border-radius: 4px 4px 0 0; margin: -14px -14px 0; }

  .flow {
    background: var(--panel-2); border: 1px dashed var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 16px 18px; margin: 26px 0 0; font-size: 12.5px;
  }
  .flow h3 { margin: 0 0 10px; font-size: 13px; }
  .flow ol { margin: 0; padding-left: 18px; }
  .flow li { margin: 5px 0; color: var(--ink); }
  .flow .muted { color: var(--muted); }

  .notecols { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 18px; margin-top: 26px; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .notecols { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .note { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 14px 16px; }
  .note h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 13px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px; }
  .note ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 16px; font-size: 12.5px; }
  .note li { margin: 4px 0; }
  .pill { font-size: 10px; padding: 1px 7px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--muted); }
  .warn { color: var(--danger); }
  .arrow-down { text-align:center; color: var(--muted); font-size: 20px; line-height:1; margin: 4px 0; }
  .midlines { display:grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr; gap:20px; margin: 6px 0 2px; }
  @media (max-width: 860px){ .midlines { grid-template-columns:1fr; } }
  .midlines .l { text-align:center; font-size:11px; color:var(--muted); }
  .midlines .l code { font-size:10.5px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">
  <h1>SlayZone — Multi-Hub Federation</h1>
  <p class="sub">One desktop client, many full-data hubs. Each hub owns its own database; each hub can drive many runner exec nodes. Commit <code>67c7e09a8</code>.</p>

  <div class="legend">
    <span><i class="dot" style="background:var(--client)"></i>Desktop client</span>
    <span><i class="dot" style="background:var(--local)"></i>Local hub (always on)</span>
    <span><i class="dot" style="background:var(--remote)"></i>Remote hub</span>
    <span><i class="dot" style="background:var(--runner)"></i>Runner (exec node)</span>
    <span><i class="dot" style="background:var(--auth)"></i>Auth / transport security</span>
  </div>

  <!-- ROW 1: THE CLIENT -->
  <div class="col-labels"><div>Desktop client (1)</div><div style="grid-column: span 2;">connects to N hubs at once</div></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <!-- Client card spans full concept but sits in col 1; we make it span all 3 for clarity -->
    <div class="card" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;">
      <div class="bar" style="background:var(--client)"></div>
      <h2><i class="dot" style="background:var(--client)"></i>Electron desktop client <span class="tag">— single app, single window</span></h2>
      <div class="body" style="grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; display:grid;">
        <div class="chip">
          <b>Main process</b>
          <div class="k">Owns cross-hub state (a hub can't store the list of hubs).</div>
          <div class="edge accent-client" style="margin-top:8px;"><code>boot-config.json</code> — hub registry: <code>multi_hub</code>, <code>hubs[]</code>, <code>default_hub_id</code></div>
          <div class="edge accent-auth"><code>hub-tokens.ts</code> — per-hub bearer tokens, <b>safeStorage-encrypted</b></div>
          <div class="edge accent-auth"><code>hub-cert-pinning.ts</code> — <code>setCertificateVerifyProc</code> pins remote wss leaf (TOFU)</div>
          <div class="edge accent-local">local sidecar supervisor — spawns the local hub</div>
        </div>
        <div class="chip">
          <b>Renderer</b>
          <div class="k">Federates over the registry; UI never picks an "active hub".</div>
          <div class="edge accent-client"><b>FederationProvider</b> — <code>Map&lt;hubId → {wsClient, queryClient}&gt;</code> (per-hub cache)</div>
          <div class="edge accent-client"><b>HubScope</b> — nested tRPC provider; a project/tab's subtree talks to its own hub</div>
          <div class="edge accent-runner"><b>PtyEventStreams</b> — live PTY streams mounted <i>per hub</i></div>
          <div class="edge accent-local"><b>useTasksData</b> — flat rail = union of every hub's projects; writes routed to owning hub</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="arrow-down">▼ ▼ ▼</div>
  <div class="midlines">
    <div class="l">client → local hub<br><code>ws://127.0.0.1/trpc</code> · no auth</div>
    <div class="l">client → remote hub<br><code>wss://…/trpc</code> · bearer + cert-pin</div>
    <div class="l">client → remote hub<br><code>wss://…/trpc</code> · bearer + cert-pin</div>
  </div>

  <!-- ROW 2: THE HUBS -->
  <div class="col-labels"><div>Local hub</div><div>Remote hub A</div><div>Remote hub B</div></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <!-- LOCAL HUB -->
    <div class="card">
      <div class="bar" style="background:var(--local)"></div>
      <h2><i class="dot" style="background:var(--local)"></i>Local hub</h2>
      <div class="tag">co-located sidecar · always present + running</div>
      <div class="body">
        <div class="chip"><b>SQLite DB</b><span class="k">its own projects · tasks · settings</span></div>
        <div class="chip"><b>tRPC routers</b><span class="k">projects, task, pty, chat, hub, runners…</span></div>
        <div class="chip"><b>Transport</b><span class="k">plain <code>ws://</code> loopback, origin-guarded</span></div>
        <div class="edge accent-auth" style="margin-top:2px;">Auth: <b>none</b> — trusted loopback (default)</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- REMOTE HUB A -->
    <div class="card">
      <div class="bar" style="background:var(--remote)"></div>
      <h2><i class="dot" style="background:var(--remote)"></i>Remote hub A</h2>
      <div class="tag">self-hosted <code>@slayzone/hub</code></div>
      <div class="body">
        <div class="chip"><b>SQLite DB</b><span class="k">its own projects · tasks · settings</span></div>
        <div class="chip"><b>tRPC routers</b> + <b>REST/MCP</b><span class="k">same app surface as local</span></div>
        <div class="chip"><b>hub-identity</b><span class="k">self-signed TLS leaf → cert fingerprint (the pin)</span></div>
        <div class="edge accent-auth" style="margin-top:2px;">Auth: <b>BetterAuth</b> bearer (opt-in via <code>SLAYZONE_HUB_AUTH_REQUIRED</code>)</div>
        <div class="edge accent-auth">https <code>/trpc</code> listener (own port) terminates TLS</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- REMOTE HUB B -->
    <div class="card">
      <div class="bar" style="background:var(--remote)"></div>
      <h2><i class="dot" style="background:var(--remote)"></i>Remote hub B</h2>
      <div class="tag">…any number of hubs</div>
      <div class="body">
        <div class="chip"><b>SQLite DB</b><span class="k">fully independent data</span></div>
        <div class="chip"><b>tRPC routers</b><span class="k">projects rendered flat in the client rail</span></div>
        <div class="edge accent-remote" style="margin-top:2px;">A project belongs to <b>exactly one</b> hub — the DB it lives in</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="arrow-down">▼ &nbsp;&nbsp; runners dial IN to their hub &nbsp;&nbsp; ▼</div>
  <div class="midlines">
    <div class="l">local runner (auto-enrolled)<br><code>wss://…/fleet</code></div>
    <div class="l">runner → hub A<br><code>wss://…/fleet</code> · join-token + cert-pin</div>
    <div class="l">runner → hub B<br><code>wss://…/fleet</code></div>
  </div>

  <!-- ROW 3: THE RUNNERS -->
  <div class="col-labels"><div>Runner(s) of local hub</div><div>Runner(s) of hub A</div><div>Runner(s) of hub B</div></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="bar" style="background:var(--runner)"></div>
      <h2><i class="dot" style="background:var(--runner)"></i>Local runner</h2>
      <div class="tag">exec node · one hub → many runners</div>
      <div class="body">
        <div class="chip"><b>Runs</b><span class="k">node-pty · git · fs · processes</span></div>
        <div class="edge accent-runner" style="margin-top:2px;">Dials OUT to its hub (NAT-friendly); hub never dials the runner</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="bar" style="background:var(--runner)"></div>
      <h2><i class="dot" style="background:var(--runner)"></i>Runner(s) — hub A</h2>
      <div class="tag">enrolled via join token</div>
      <div class="body">
        <div class="chip"><b>Exec only</b><span class="k">data stays in hub A's DB</span></div>
        <div class="edge accent-runner" style="margin-top:2px;">A task binds to a runner; unbound → runs in the hub process</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="bar" style="background:var(--runner)"></div>
      <h2><i class="dot" style="background:var(--runner)"></i>Runner(s) — hub B</h2>
      <div class="tag">independent fleet</div>
      <div class="body">
        <div class="chip"><b>Exec only</b><span class="k">pty/git/fs on hub B's machines</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- CONNECTION / DATA FLOW -->
  <div class="flow">
    <h3>How a project on a remote hub behaves</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Client's <b>FederationProvider</b> opens one WebSocket + QueryClient <span class="muted">per hub</span> (local reuses the boot singleton).</li>
      <li><b>useTasksData</b> fetches every hub's project list and merges them into <b>one flat rail</b> — each row tagged with its origin hub.</li>
      <li>You click a remote project → its board/tab renders inside that hub's <b>HubScope</b>, so all <code>useTRPC()</code> calls resolve to <b>that hub</b>.</li>
      <li>A task write (move / edit / archive) is <b>routed to the owning hub's client</b> — never the wrong DB.</li>
      <li>Its terminal spawns on that hub (and optionally on one of that hub's <b>runners</b>); the hub's PTY stream feeds the client's per-hub <b>PtyEventStreams</b>.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <!-- NOTES: two axes + auth -->
  <div class="notecols">
    <div class="note">
      <h3><i class="dot" style="background:var(--remote)"></i>Two different axes — don't conflate</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Federation</b> = <b>one client → many hubs</b>. Hubs are peers; each owns full data.</li>
        <li><b>Fleet</b> = <b>one hub → many runners</b>. Runners are exec-only; data stays in the hub.</li>
        <li>So the local machine is: a client <i>and</i> a hub <i>and</i> (usually) that hub's runner.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="note">
      <h3><i class="dot" style="background:var(--auth)"></i>Auth &amp; transport security</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Local hub:</b> loopback, no auth (trusted). Default everywhere unless a hub opts in.</li>
        <li><b>Remote hub:</b> <code>wss://</code> + cert pinning (pinned in <b>main</b> — the renderer WS has no cert hook) + <b>bearer via tRPC connectionParams</b> → <code>verifySession</code>.</li>
        <li><span class="pill">status</span> Auth is <b>attributive today</b>: the hub attaches <code>ctx.principal</code> but <span class="warn">no procedure requires it yet</span>. Login UI + procedure gating are the remaining pieces.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
